  "body": "Maintainer request from #1452 (\"We should be able to load DXF file to do profile cuts on.\").\n\n## Goal\nBuild a clean-room ASCII DXF reader in `crates/geometry/src/dxf/`. Read Autodesk's published DXF Reference only. Add zero new external crate dependencies. Keep the API neutral so #743 and #744 can share it later.\n\n## Scope\n- Parse DXF sections `HEADER`, `TABLES`, and `ENTITIES`.\n- Read `$INSUNITS` explicitly as `Known(Unit)` (inch code `1`, millimeter code `4`, plus standard length scales), `MissingOrUnitless` (`0` or absent), or `Unsupported(i32)`. Never guess millimeters vs inches on missing units.\n- Read `LAYER` definitions and keep layer names on every extracted primitive.\n- Parse 2D primitives `LINE`, `ARC`, `CIRCLE`, `LWPOLYLINE`, and `POLYLINE`/`VERTEX`/`SEQEND`. Convert group-42 bulges into exact `Arc` segments and keep `ARC` and `CIRCLE` exact without polygonizing.\n- Skip `TEXT`, `MTEXT`, `DIMENSION`, and `HATCH`, and count skipped entities per kind in an import summary struct.\n- Reject non-planar extrusion vectors (`210`, `220`, `230` tilted away from `+Z`) or varying Z heights by name.\n- Guard untrusted input strictly: detect and refuse Binary DXF (`AutoCAD Binary DXF`) headers, enforce maximum file size, entity count, and vertex count caps before bulk allocation, reject NaN/Inf or coordinates past `geo2d::COORD_LIMIT`, drop or refuse zero-length entities safely, and use zero `unwrap`/`expect`/`panic!`.\n- Leave `SPLINE`, `ELLIPSE`, and `BLOCK`/`INSERT` to the follow-up curve/block sub-issue, refusing them by DXF entity name for now.\n\n## Done means\nTests parse valid ASCII DXFs with rectangles, circles, arcs, bulges, layers, and `$INSUNITS` into exact primitives; tests refuse binary files, malformed group codes, truncated streams, unsupported entities, tilted extrusions, NaN values, and oversized counts by name; a deterministic smoke-fuzz test runs with zero panics.\n\nPart of #1452\n",
